import wb_dma_hs_pkg::*;

// The hardware-handshake operation model, one instance per handshake-capable
// channel (§4, ``dma_hs_c``).
//
// The participant here is the PERIPHERAL DEVICE, not the processor: this is the
// model a device-side consumer -- or a requesting IP's own operation model --
// composes with. That is why it lives in ``tests/pss`` rather than in the device
// tree.
//
// All three of its operations are end-to-end or configuration with no polling
// half. A sideband has no state to poll, so its operations arrive at the right
// shape naturally.
//
// **No base address, and that absence is the point:** this interface has no
// address space at all, which is what distinguishes a sideband from a bus
// interface.
//
// None of the three is ever a driver state. ``request_chunk()`` waits on a pin
// with no processor involved, and ``dma_nd_i`` / ``dma_rest_i`` have no register
// bit anywhere in §4, so software cannot invoke them at all.
component wb_dma_hs_c {

    // Index into ``dma_req_i`` / ``dma_ack_o`` / ``dma_nd_i`` / ``dma_rest_i``.
    //
    // Set by the environment during initialization, and passed to every foreign
    // function this component calls.
    int     chan;

    // How far ``dma_nd_i`` must lead ``dma_req_i``, in cycles.
    //
    // §3.9 requires at least two.
    int     nd_lead_cycles = 2;
}
